    "body": "@jakearchibald @youennf @rayankans does any of you think this boolean is worth having for CORS? I think I'd rather allow whitespace in CORS for the `Range` header so we can keep `Range` header parsing consistent. In particular this would allow an arbitrary number of 0x09 and 0x20 after `bytes=`. I don't see the security benefit.\r\n\r\n(We also use this parser for `blob:` URL requests and there we already allow whitespace.)",
